<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.16.3: Quadratic Equations and Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02030</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.16.3: Quadratic Equations and Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>90aa626a-3928-45c0-9ec3-536bbe4c6592</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><figure><media alt="GRAPHS A THROUGH F. GRAPH A IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (4, 1). GRAPH B IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 1, NEGATIVE 4). GRAPH C IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS DOWN WITH A VERTEX AT (4, 1). GRAPH D IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS DOWN WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 1, NEGATIVE 4). GRAPH E IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 4, NEGATIVE 1). GRAPH F IS A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH A VERTEX AT (1, 4)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f38d59f200df6a983128aa7f5619f7153bdd8c78"/></media></figure><link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f38d59f200df6a983128aa7f5619f7153bdd8c78">Moodle 6.16.3 Image of all 6 graphs</link></para>
<para>Your teacher will give you a <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/731925b6969bc490346728eef9715f3856fc95f1">set of cards</link>. Each card contains an equation or a graph that represents a quadratic function. Take turns matching each equation to a graph that represents the same function.</para>
<list>
  <item> For each pair of cards that you match, explain to your partner how you know they belong together. </item>
  <item> For each pair of cards that your partner matches, listen carefully to their explanation. If you disagree, discuss your thinking and work to reach an agreement. </item>
  <item> Once all the cards are matched, record the equation, the letter of the equation, and a sketch of the corresponding graph, and write a brief note or explanation about how you knew they were a match. </item>
</list>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="a5a39f83-9dbe-449a-a961-b24d10d83459"><problem><para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/9e3666853195ea17931a06f0d3d0c0ea93498bf8"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Choose the equation that matches this graph.</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(f(x)=(x−1)^2+4\)</para><para>\(g(x)=-(x−4)^2+1\)</para><para>\(h(x)=(x+1)^2−4\) </para><para>\(p(x)=-(x+1)^2−4\)</para><para>\(q(x)=2(x−4)^2+1\)</para><para>\(r(x)=(x+4)^2−1\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(f(x)=(x−1)^2+4\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(f(x)=(x−1)^2+4\)</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
